WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.200
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:04.000
We're here with the one,
the only Alan Cumming.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.634
And, obviously,
a job like yours requires

00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:08.133
a little bit of discretion
on a show like this.

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:10.634
Are you a
good keeper of secrets?

00:00:10.634 --> 00:00:11.934
-Uh, what do you think?

00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:13.367
No.

00:00:13.367 --> 00:00:15.767
-You seem like someone who would
really enjoy telling a secret.

00:00:15.767 --> 00:00:16.767
-I love it.
-Yeah.

00:00:16.767 --> 00:00:17.834
-I can't keep secrets.

00:00:17.834 --> 00:00:21.501
You know, like,
my worst one was --

00:00:21.501 --> 00:00:22.634
You know in "The Good --"
Remember in "The Good Wife"?

00:00:22.634 --> 00:00:23.901
-Yeah.
-I was in that.

00:00:23.901 --> 00:00:26.868
And there was a bit
when Will got shot and died.

00:00:26.868 --> 00:00:28.467
Will was,
you know, the leading guy,

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:31.133
and Alicia was his --
They were having an affair.

00:00:31.133 --> 00:00:32.367
It was all this big thing.

00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:34.934
And he gets shot,
and it was a big thing.

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:36.901
And it was
actually one of these things --

00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:39.000
it was hard to believe they
actually could keep it a secret,

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.234
because when it went out on TV,

00:00:40.234 --> 00:00:41.501
the whole country was like,
"What?!"

00:00:41.501 --> 00:00:42.534
-Yep. It was a big deal.
It was the kind of character

00:00:42.534 --> 00:00:43.701
you didn't think
would get killed off.

00:00:43.701 --> 00:00:46.367
-Well, I was also surprised that
nobody found out,

00:00:46.367 --> 00:00:47.734
because I told everybody.

00:00:47.734 --> 00:00:52.234
And I was -- I just --
I just couldn't keep it secret.

00:00:52.234 --> 00:00:53.334
I was just -- People would say,

00:00:53.334 --> 00:00:54.601
"Oh, hey,
I really love 'The Good Wife.'"

00:00:54.601 --> 00:00:56.067
"Will's going to die."

00:00:56.067 --> 00:00:58.434
And there was
one time when I was --

00:00:58.434 --> 00:01:01.167
I was doing a fashion thing
and I sat down

00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:02.501
to get my
hair and makeup done,

00:01:02.501 --> 00:01:05.000
and the hair guy --
And I told the hairdresser.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.400
I just -- I mean, never tell
hairdressers secrets.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:11.100
They're worse than me.
But I just told everybody.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.567
It was like a sort of --
What's that thing where you --

00:01:13.567 --> 00:01:14.701
Tourette's, you know?

00:01:14.701 --> 00:01:17.133
-Yeah.
You got secrets Tourette's.

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:19.000
-But nobody found out.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.234
-Wow! Unbelievable.
-Yeah.

00:01:20.234 --> 00:01:21.300
-You told the right people.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:22.400
You told the right people
your secrets.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.801
-Yes, I'm choosey, I suppose.
Yeah.

00:01:24.801 --> 00:01:26.667
-You have a film coming out
called "Marlowe" --

00:01:26.667 --> 00:01:30.200
a fantastic cast -- Liam Neeson,
Diane Kruger, Jessica Lange.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:31.934
You've worked with
Jessica Lange before.

00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:33.767
-Several times, actually.
She's an absolute hoot.

00:01:33.767 --> 00:01:35.667
And, you know, it's
Liam Neeson's 100th film.

00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:36.834
-Wow!
-Isn't that incredible?

00:01:36.834 --> 00:01:39.100
-That's a really
nice thing to hit.

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:40.100
-Yes. And it was lovely.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.901
We made it in Barcelona,

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:45.067
pretending to be L.A.
in the '30s.

00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:46.868
And, yeah -- And I love --

00:01:46.868 --> 00:01:50.701
Jessica Lange and I -- we did
"Titus" and we did another one.

00:01:50.701 --> 00:01:51.968
And she's hilarious.

00:01:51.968 --> 00:01:53.467
I actually talk about her
in my new --

00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:54.834
my concert show
that I've been doing.

00:01:54.834 --> 00:01:56.067
I was just in Australia.

00:01:56.067 --> 00:01:58.000
It's called "Alan Cumming
Is Not Acting His Age."

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.434
And I tell this story about
how, one time,

00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:01.767
we were making -- doing "Titus."

00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:03.501
And you know, like,
in the middle of filming,

00:02:03.501 --> 00:02:05.834
you're hanging around,
you're chatting, and gossiping.

00:02:05.834 --> 00:02:07.968
And we were talking --
Jessica and I were talking about

00:02:07.968 --> 00:02:11.300
the way -- the effects of
gravity on your body.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:12.767
-As you get older.
-Exactly.

00:02:12.767 --> 00:02:15.334
And she was saying that her
boobs were getting a bit saggy.

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:17.634
I said, "Well, my balls have
gone south, let me tell you."

00:02:17.634 --> 00:02:20.033
And so we were
having a laugh about that.

00:02:20.033 --> 00:02:23.234
Then, weeks later,
we were doing this other scene

00:02:23.234 --> 00:02:25.534
where we're naked, and I'm sort
of asleep on top of her.

00:02:25.534 --> 00:02:26.868
And I'm lying on top of her.

00:02:26.868 --> 00:02:28.234
There's one hand on her boob,
and I'm sort of asleep

00:02:28.234 --> 00:02:29.334
on her chest.

00:02:29.334 --> 00:02:31.634
And having a laugh
in between takes.

00:02:31.634 --> 00:02:33.968
And she -- At one point,
I say to her,

00:02:33.968 --> 00:02:36.100
"Gosh, Jess, you know, I don't
know what you're talking about.

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:37.634
You have fantastic boobs."

00:02:37.634 --> 00:02:39.834
And she said, "Honey,
if your hand wasn't there,

00:02:39.834 --> 00:02:41.667
that thing would be
halfway around my back."

00:02:41.667 --> 00:02:44.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.701 --> 00:02:49.534
-Do you think,
at this point, people are like,

00:02:49.534 --> 00:02:51.868
"I want to give Alan
a really good story

00:02:51.868 --> 00:02:53.767
so I can make
his next one-man show"?

00:02:53.767 --> 00:02:55.100
-Yes.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:57.734
-I feel like people talk to you
the way they talk

00:02:57.734 --> 00:02:59.934
in, like, 1950,
like, banter films.

00:02:59.934 --> 00:03:01.234
-It is a bit like that.

00:03:01.234 --> 00:03:03.934
But, also, like, it's bizarrely
because I do have

00:03:03.934 --> 00:03:06.767
a problem keeping secrets --
or I do keep, like,

00:03:06.767 --> 00:03:08.434
when it's a proper secret,
if someone doesn't want me

00:03:08.434 --> 00:03:09.734
to tell something.

00:03:09.734 --> 00:03:12.634
But things like that, I do --
I'm sort of mouthy.

00:03:12.634 --> 00:03:15.567
But also, conversely,
people tell me things.

00:03:15.567 --> 00:03:18.601
Like, I've got -- I think people
feel comfortable

00:03:18.601 --> 00:03:20.701
to tell me
their innermost secrets.

00:03:20.701 --> 00:03:23.033
-It seems like maybe a bad call.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:26.968
-[ Humming ]
-Oh, no!

00:03:26.968 --> 00:03:28.968
We got to get out of here
before I tell you something.

00:03:28.968 --> 00:03:30.300
Hey, it's always such
a pleasure to see you.

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:31.534
Congratulations on the show.
-Thank you.

00:03:31.534 --> 00:03:33.000
-Alan Cumming!

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.767
"The Traitors"
streaming now on Peacock.

00:03:34.767 --> 00:03:36.300
We'll be right back with
Jonathan Groff.

